# Horse Model Loading Performance Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Keep the existing `Models::load()` / `Renderer::ModelScene::instantiate()` API while moving glTF texture decode/derivation off the caller thread and adding a transparent compiled model cache.

**Architecture:** Model geometry and metadata remain synchronously published so existing `ModelHandle` semantics do not change. glTF import registers stable deferred texture handles; a generic internal worker pool decodes/derives textures and writes model-cache payloads, while main-thread resource pumping commits completions and advances `Models::resourceRevision()`. A platform cache stores normalized Horse model data and dependency metadata so warm loads bypass source glTF reconstruction.

**Tech Stack:** C++20, Horse Models/Renderer/ECS systems, SDL_GPU resource fallback, C-BuildSystem, standard-library threads/filesystem/binary I/O.

**Spec:** `MODEL_LOADING_DESIGN`

## Global Constraints

- Horse-only change; do not modify GAME.
- Keep `Models::load(path)` and `Renderer::ModelScene::instantiate(...)` unchanged for callers.
- Keep geometry/model publication synchronous in this phase.
- Worker threads must not mutate ECS, GPU state, model/mesh/material registries, or published texture assets.
- Pending/failed textures use the renderer fallback and must not make a valid model fail.
- Reuse `Models::resourceRevision()` and shared scene-resource synchronization rather than backend-specific streaming systems.
- Cache corruption or cache-write failure must never prevent source loading.
- No `docs/superpowers` tree; project documentation stays at repository root.

---

## File Structure

- `Sources/Core/Jobs/Jobs.hpp` / `Jobs.cpp`: generic bounded CPU worker pool and completion queue.
- `Sources/Models/Internal/TextureStreaming.hpp` / `TextureStreaming.cpp`: deferred texture descriptors, dependency scheduling, generation safety, main-thread commit.
- `Sources/Models/Core/Texture.cpp` / `Texture.hpp`: stable texture assets and existing synchronous texture API; internal streaming hooks delegate into the new runtime.
- `Sources/Models/Formats/GltfAssets.cpp`: register file/memory/channel texture sources without decoding them during import.
- `Sources/Models/Formats/GltfAlpha.cpp`: register alpha-derived textures without synchronous image copies.
- `Sources/Models/Internal/ModelCache.hpp` / `ModelCache.cpp`: platform cache root, dependency manifest, binary read/write, validation and atomic replacement.
- `Sources/Models/Models.cpp`: cache-first model load path and generation-safe clear.
- `Sources/Renderer/Scenes/SceneCache.cpp`: shared main-thread resource completion pump before resource signatures are evaluated.
- `Sources/Renderer/Scenes/SceneResourcesSDLGPU.cpp`: use the existing white texture for pending/failed CPU textures rather than returning a scene error.
- `Tests/ModelLoading.cpp`: deterministic regression coverage for jobs, deferred textures, cache validation and stale-generation rejection.
- `build.c`: compile `Sources/Core/*/*.cpp`, add the model-loading test executable, keep Horse as the default target.

